<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Wage deal ends Nestle S.Africa strike.</title>
<headline>Wage deal ends Nestle S.Africa strike.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A four-week strike for higher pay by about 2,800 workers at 10 South African factories of food and beverage group Nestle SA has ended following an agreement reached on Monday, the Swiss-based company said.</p>
<p>The wage deal with the Food and Allied Workers Union (FAWU) includes a minimum increase of 9.0 percent, resulting in a minimum wage of 2,300 rand a month.</p>
<p>The increase has been linked to productivity issues which Nestle said would enhance its competitive position.</p>
<p>Nestle employs 6,000 workers nationally. Those not on strike continued with their normal duty.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
